1
00:01:29,990 --> 00:01:35,610
It'll be impossible for us to eat all this.

2
00:01:59,990 --> 00:02:12,050
Oh, there you are.

3
00:02:13,490 --> 00:02:15,430
Why do you look like that?

4
00:02:16,130 --> 00:02:19,330
I thought I gave you a mission to search for His Majesty.

5
00:02:20,850 --> 00:02:23,670
I do not recall allowing you to rest.

6
00:02:23,670 --> 00:02:30,650
What the hell was that?

7
00:02:31,470 --> 00:02:33,910
My sword just fell from against the wall.

8
00:02:34,510 --> 00:02:36,710
Tie that stupid thing up already.

9
00:02:38,770 --> 00:02:39,530
Fallon?

10
00:02:40,730 --> 00:02:42,550
Marcel. Marcel!

11
00:02:44,490 --> 00:02:45,610
Where's Fallon?

12
00:02:46,330 --> 00:02:47,670
Uh, what?

13
00:02:48,850 --> 00:02:51,050
Hey, have you seen Fallon anywhere?

14
00:02:51,390 --> 00:02:52,970
Can't say anyone's passed by.

15
00:02:53,990 --> 00:02:56,510
What? Did something happen?

16
00:02:57,750 --> 00:02:59,030
It can't be.

17
00:03:00,170 --> 00:03:01,890
Did she leave from this window?

18
00:03:05,170 --> 00:03:06,730
I'm gonna look outside.

19
00:03:07,790 --> 00:03:08,190
Huh?

20
00:03:18,050 --> 00:03:19,670
Why is it...

21
00:03:19,670 --> 00:03:21,290
Fallon!

22
00:03:21,290 --> 00:03:24,450
Hey, what's wrong?

23
00:03:25,410 --> 00:03:26,510
Are you...

24
00:03:26,510 --> 00:03:31,310
Are you okay? Tell me what happened.

25
00:03:32,210 --> 00:03:33,410
I must find him.

26
00:03:34,390 --> 00:03:36,130
I must find Lord Delgall.

27
00:03:36,710 --> 00:03:37,450
Wait a sec.

28
00:03:38,210 --> 00:03:38,790
How...

29
00:03:38,790 --> 00:03:40,010
In this kingdom...

30
00:03:40,010 --> 00:03:42,010
Everything that you can see...

31
00:03:43,010 --> 00:03:44,010
Buildings...

32
00:03:44,010 --> 00:03:45,010
Currency...

33
00:03:45,010 --> 00:03:46,010
Livestock...

34
00:03:46,010 --> 00:03:47,010
Citizens...

35
00:03:47,010 --> 00:03:48,010
Blood...

36
00:03:48,010 --> 00:03:49,010
And meat.

37
00:03:49,010 --> 00:03:54,650
Even each and every tiny grain of sand that you crush beneath your feet.

38
00:03:54,650 --> 00:03:59,210
All of it is the personal property of his majesty, King Delgall.

39
00:03:59,210 --> 00:04:00,810
And only his.

40
00:04:02,870 --> 00:04:05,670
Do you understand, you disgusting thief?

41
00:04:05,670 --> 00:04:07,510
You.

42
00:04:07,510 --> 00:04:09,090
I remember you.

43
00:04:09,090 --> 00:04:12,230
You were wandering around in the paintings.

44
00:04:12,890 --> 00:04:13,890
The paintings?

45
00:04:14,490 --> 00:04:15,570
That's right.

46
00:04:16,190 --> 00:04:17,410
But who is he?

47
00:04:17,410 --> 00:04:19,770
You vile intruder.

48
00:04:20,250 --> 00:04:21,950
Just what is it that you want?

49
00:04:25,950 --> 00:04:27,670
It's the Lord of the Dungeon.

50
00:04:28,910 --> 00:04:30,370
The Mad Mage himself.

51
00:04:34,570 --> 00:04:35,130
You.

52
00:04:35,350 --> 00:04:36,530
You get away from them.

53
00:04:36,850 --> 00:04:37,590
Do you hear me?

54
00:04:38,130 --> 00:04:39,270
I won't miss again.

55
00:04:39,270 --> 00:04:44,710
You should know your place, you filth.

56
00:04:46,050 --> 00:04:47,090
Hey, let's go.

57
00:04:47,550 --> 00:04:47,970
Come on.

58
00:04:49,970 --> 00:04:50,930
Shut up!

59
00:04:55,430 --> 00:04:56,030
L-Laios!

60
00:04:56,330 --> 00:04:58,230
Such amazing strength.

61
00:04:58,230 --> 00:05:00,690
What the hell is going on here?

62
00:05:01,090 --> 00:05:02,290
Is he an adventurer?

63
00:05:05,690 --> 00:05:06,290
Spellbook?

64
00:05:06,670 --> 00:05:08,690
I have a bad feeling about this.

65
00:05:08,690 --> 00:05:14,030
Is that some kind of magic chant?

66
00:05:17,030 --> 00:05:19,470
This chanting could only be...

67
00:05:19,470 --> 00:05:25,230
Ancient magic!

68
00:05:25,810 --> 00:05:27,010
To bury them all!

69
00:05:36,010 --> 00:05:37,090
Explosion magic.

70
00:05:37,350 --> 00:05:38,230
Abjuration magic.

71
00:05:38,230 --> 00:05:39,910
No, those won't work.

72
00:05:40,810 --> 00:05:41,230
Then...

73
00:05:47,810 --> 00:05:50,330
I'll overwrite the spell instead.

74
00:05:58,390 --> 00:05:59,070
Dispel!

75
00:05:59,070 --> 00:06:05,650
Dispel!

76
00:06:08,650 --> 00:06:10,150
This ancient magic?

77
00:06:10,550 --> 00:06:11,930
I can understand it.

78
00:06:11,970 --> 00:06:13,010
I can read it.

79
00:06:13,110 --> 00:06:13,650
But...

80
00:06:13,650 --> 00:06:19,450
I can't keep up with it!

81
00:06:19,450 --> 00:06:42,970
Are you the one who made this dungeon?

82
00:06:42,970 --> 00:06:43,970
I need...

83
00:06:43,970 --> 00:06:45,550
I need...

84
00:06:45,550 --> 00:06:46,970
To talk to you about...

85
00:06:46,970 --> 00:06:47,790
I...

86
00:06:47,790 --> 00:07:08,690
Don't look so worried.

87
00:07:08,690 --> 00:07:10,630
The thieves are gone now.

88
00:07:10,630 --> 00:07:15,350
And his majesty will soon be returning.

89
00:07:15,990 --> 00:07:18,050
When he does, we'll be sure to celebrate.

90
00:07:20,370 --> 00:07:21,390
Hey, dragon.

91
00:07:24,650 --> 00:07:26,330
That must be inconvenient.

92
00:07:26,330 --> 00:07:29,390
Let me change your form for you.

93
00:07:29,390 --> 00:07:40,510
Do what you have been ordered to.

94
00:07:43,010 --> 00:07:43,390
Yes.

95
00:07:43,390 --> 00:07:49,770
What happened?

96
00:07:49,770 --> 00:07:51,130
Hold on.

97
00:07:51,250 --> 00:07:52,190
I'll get lights up.

98
00:07:52,190 --> 00:07:57,750
What is this place?

99
00:07:58,070 --> 00:08:00,170
Come to think of it, where did we fall from?

100
00:08:00,790 --> 00:08:01,910
How do we leave?

101
00:08:02,370 --> 00:08:03,370
There's no...

102
00:08:03,370 --> 00:08:05,870
What's happening?

103
00:08:05,870 --> 00:08:06,830
Oh, no.

104
00:08:07,090 --> 00:08:08,530
Are the walls closing in?

105
00:08:08,730 --> 00:08:10,110
You've got to be kidding me!

106
00:08:10,470 --> 00:08:10,870
Dammit!

107
00:08:11,170 --> 00:08:12,190
We've got to look for an exit!

108
00:08:12,410 --> 00:08:12,850
Where?

109
00:08:13,370 --> 00:08:15,270
Can't you fix it with magic or something?

110
00:08:15,470 --> 00:08:17,250
And what kind of magic do you suggest?

111
00:08:25,750 --> 00:08:26,690
We're dead.

112
00:08:27,390 --> 00:08:31,770
This won't be my first time dying, but no one is going to find us under rocks.

113
00:08:32,510 --> 00:08:34,530
We just got Fallon back.

114
00:08:34,530 --> 00:08:37,230
And I was so close to the dungeon's secrets.

115
00:08:37,810 --> 00:08:39,230
It'll have been for nothing.

116
00:08:40,550 --> 00:08:42,690
It can't end like this.

117
00:08:47,270 --> 00:08:48,270
Marcel, no!

118
00:08:49,950 --> 00:08:51,230
Whoa, it's a tunnel!

119
00:08:51,530 --> 00:08:52,710
Let's use it to get out!

120
00:08:53,450 --> 00:08:55,390
What, we don't even know where it ends up?

121
00:08:55,870 --> 00:08:57,790
It's better than becoming a pancake!

122
00:08:58,270 --> 00:09:00,210
Just hurry up and go!

123
00:09:04,530 --> 00:09:10,690
Where the hell are we?

124
00:09:13,810 --> 00:09:16,330
Wherever it is, we've got to get out and fast.

125
00:09:16,330 --> 00:09:21,150
I... I can't even move a finger right now.

126
00:09:21,290 --> 00:09:22,770
You've got to get up!

127
00:09:23,290 --> 00:09:25,330
If that guy finds us again, we're...

128
00:09:25,330 --> 00:09:34,830
It's... it's over.

129
00:09:34,830 --> 00:09:35,830
It's over.

130
00:09:37,670 --> 00:09:39,970
It's over.

131
00:09:42,310 --> 00:09:44,370
There's no need to...

132
00:09:44,370 --> 00:09:49,290
They... they disappeared?

133
00:09:49,950 --> 00:09:51,030
Ugh, damn it.

134
00:09:51,410 --> 00:09:52,810
I think I'm going crazy.

135
00:09:54,750 --> 00:09:57,610
Senshi, I need you to wake up Lyos for me.

136
00:09:57,970 --> 00:10:00,070
I'm gonna go look around a little bit.

137
00:10:00,070 --> 00:10:07,150
Get him!

138
00:10:07,350 --> 00:10:09,070
How did he manage to sneak in here?

139
00:10:09,470 --> 00:10:10,990
The long ears with them!

140
00:10:11,290 --> 00:10:12,130
There he is!

141
00:10:12,330 --> 00:10:13,090
Come here, you!

142
00:10:13,730 --> 00:10:14,730
Quiet down!

143
00:10:15,590 --> 00:10:16,670
What's going on?

144
00:10:17,030 --> 00:10:18,430
We found some moles, Captain.

145
00:10:18,790 --> 00:10:19,790
How'd they get in here?

146
00:10:20,250 --> 00:10:21,790
Why'd the watch not catch them?

147
00:10:22,350 --> 00:10:24,370
To be honest, we don't know.

148
00:10:24,790 --> 00:10:26,310
The hole's closed up now.

149
00:10:26,530 --> 00:10:26,950
Whatever.

150
00:10:26,950 --> 00:10:35,190
A tiny man, an underground dweller, a long legs, and a long ear.

151
00:10:35,710 --> 00:10:36,430
How perfect!

152
00:10:37,030 --> 00:10:40,630
I've never killed a long ear before, but now I can.

153
00:10:40,970 --> 00:10:42,830
Give the small one to the dogs.

154
00:10:43,290 --> 00:10:44,730
They're starved for entertainment.

155
00:10:45,690 --> 00:10:46,050
Wait.

156
00:10:46,270 --> 00:10:49,770
You wouldn't happen to be Chief Zone's younger sister, would you, Miss?

157
00:10:49,770 --> 00:10:54,390
The reason we came here was actually to fulfill a promise with the Chief.

158
00:10:55,150 --> 00:10:56,470
So mind showing us mercy?

159
00:10:58,210 --> 00:10:59,850
How do you know that name?

160
00:11:05,230 --> 00:11:05,950
Hold on.

161
00:11:06,130 --> 00:11:06,810
We know you.

162
00:11:07,070 --> 00:11:09,310
You're since way different, vegetable seller.

163
00:11:10,150 --> 00:11:12,750
It must have been important for you to come this far.

164
00:11:12,750 --> 00:11:15,310
What was the promise you made with him?

165
00:11:17,530 --> 00:11:18,410
I see.

166
00:11:18,870 --> 00:11:21,090
Things are making a lot more sense now.

167
00:11:21,550 --> 00:11:25,170
I did think it was weird that the dragon didn't seem to be around anymore.

168
00:11:26,310 --> 00:11:28,390
In place of my brother, I thank you.

169
00:11:29,050 --> 00:11:30,070
Go prepare the medicine!

170
00:11:30,070 --> 00:11:39,870
It's ready.

171
00:11:39,870 --> 00:11:39,930
It's ready.

172
00:12:00,070 --> 00:12:19,210
Oh, hey.

173
00:12:20,070 --> 00:12:22,530
We were attacked by a magic-using elf earlier.

174
00:12:23,830 --> 00:12:24,570
You know anything?

175
00:12:25,030 --> 00:12:25,810
Like, maybe...

176
00:12:25,810 --> 00:12:27,110
What did the elf look like?

177
00:12:27,450 --> 00:12:29,770
Oh, uh, he had brown skin?

178
00:12:29,770 --> 00:12:30,830
And silver hair?

179
00:12:30,950 --> 00:12:31,590
That's him.

180
00:12:32,130 --> 00:12:34,270
I can't say I know many details.

181
00:12:35,090 --> 00:12:38,430
What I do know is, he was here long before we were.

182
00:12:38,670 --> 00:12:40,410
And seems to rule over the dungeon.

183
00:12:41,030 --> 00:12:45,090
If someone from the outside starts to meddle with the dungeon more than necessary,

184
00:12:45,650 --> 00:12:46,970
then he appears.

185
00:12:47,590 --> 00:12:50,190
He creates monsters and controls them.

186
00:12:50,690 --> 00:12:51,650
Changes the terrain.

187
00:12:52,250 --> 00:12:55,190
And can kill anything simply by opening that buck.

188
00:12:56,390 --> 00:12:58,130
Wait, he rules over the dungeon?

189
00:12:58,130 --> 00:13:01,630
So then, that was the mad mage?

190
00:13:01,950 --> 00:13:03,950
We've caught the attention of the mad mage?

191
00:13:04,430 --> 00:13:05,510
You've gotta be kidding.

192
00:13:06,210 --> 00:13:07,950
Dammit, we need to get out of here now!

193
00:13:09,190 --> 00:13:11,450
Did Marcel's magic call him to us?

194
00:13:11,990 --> 00:13:14,030
Or is it because we killed the dragon?

195
00:13:14,030 --> 00:13:17,170
He has several monsters working under him.

196
00:13:17,490 --> 00:13:20,370
If you killed one of them, then you probably made him angry.

197
00:13:21,150 --> 00:13:26,770
To protect us from that fate, my brother made sure to tell us never to touch the red dragon.

198
00:13:27,650 --> 00:13:29,410
Brother's right about everything.

199
00:13:29,890 --> 00:13:30,690
That bastard!

200
00:13:30,690 --> 00:13:34,950
When they wake up, they'll definitely want to start looking for Fallon.

201
00:13:36,090 --> 00:13:38,550
I need to make them give up no matter the cost.

202
00:13:38,870 --> 00:13:39,670
What'll you do?

203
00:13:40,510 --> 00:13:41,650
Whatever it takes.

204
00:13:41,790 --> 00:13:43,090
Burn the staff to ashes.

205
00:13:43,290 --> 00:13:45,070
Say we saw Fallon head for the surface.

206
00:13:45,570 --> 00:13:48,450
Or tell them she was satisfied after eating the dragon meat.

207
00:13:48,450 --> 00:13:51,150
So you plan to lie to him?

208
00:13:51,830 --> 00:13:53,030
Of course I do!

209
00:13:53,330 --> 00:13:56,190
If I don't lie, then those two idiots are never gonna give up!

210
00:13:56,710 --> 00:13:59,490
If we go any further, then we're definitely gonna get killed.

211
00:14:00,110 --> 00:14:01,870
Do you want to become part of the wall?

212
00:14:02,090 --> 00:14:03,170
Cause I sure don't!

213
00:14:03,730 --> 00:14:04,450
I...

214
00:14:04,450 --> 00:14:12,830
There's absolutely no way I'm dying with those two.

215
00:14:14,510 --> 00:14:15,990
Hey, uh...

216
00:14:15,990 --> 00:14:18,190
I'd like to go grab what we left behind.

217
00:14:18,870 --> 00:14:20,330
Would you mind taking me there?

218
00:14:23,450 --> 00:14:24,610
Yes, I mind.

219
00:14:24,930 --> 00:14:27,850
The stench of your cowardly nature might rub off on me.

220
00:14:28,350 --> 00:14:28,510
What?

221
00:14:29,230 --> 00:14:30,910
I'm asking you to...

222
00:14:30,910 --> 00:14:32,310
Can you please take him back?

223
00:14:32,310 --> 00:14:36,110
He is a coward, but he's not a bad person.

224
00:14:36,870 --> 00:14:37,350
Senshi!

225
00:14:37,650 --> 00:14:38,910
You're not coming along?

226
00:14:39,450 --> 00:14:42,370
Someone needs to stay by Laios and Marcil's side.

227
00:14:43,030 --> 00:14:43,290
What?

228
00:14:47,790 --> 00:14:50,190
If it's coming from you, I can't argue.

229
00:14:50,990 --> 00:14:52,230
I hate it, but fine.

230
00:14:52,350 --> 00:14:53,230
I'll guide him there.

231
00:15:00,810 --> 00:15:01,490
Damn it.

232
00:15:02,310 --> 00:15:05,350
I can't believe I'm surrounded by such idiots!

233
00:15:06,090 --> 00:15:07,430
So you lost a companion?

234
00:15:08,490 --> 00:15:09,530
We sure did.

235
00:15:10,110 --> 00:15:13,950
The last time we saw her, she had collapsed not that far from the Mad Mage.

236
00:15:14,390 --> 00:15:15,910
It's hard to be optimistic.

237
00:15:17,590 --> 00:15:20,350
Still no excuse to lie to the rest of your party.

238
00:15:21,710 --> 00:15:24,270
It's easy when it's not your problem, huh?

239
00:15:25,270 --> 00:15:26,750
I was only kidding!

240
00:15:28,090 --> 00:15:28,950
Behind you.

241
00:15:28,950 --> 00:15:37,410
Just relax.

242
00:15:38,410 --> 00:15:40,250
They're this town's residence.

243
00:15:41,450 --> 00:15:46,530
The ghosts that reside in this area are still sane, and only appear when they want to be seen.

244
00:15:47,670 --> 00:15:49,930
The paths that they travel are safe.

245
00:15:50,590 --> 00:15:51,190
Let's follow.

246
00:15:51,190 --> 00:15:56,570
Are you serious?

247
00:15:56,570 --> 00:16:08,550
Down there.

248
00:16:09,030 --> 00:16:10,530
That's where we were before.

249
00:16:11,170 --> 00:16:12,830
But the red dragon is gone.

250
00:16:14,010 --> 00:16:16,910
Did it come back to life, maybe?

251
00:16:16,910 --> 00:16:17,670
No.

252
00:16:18,190 --> 00:16:20,530
The dogs don't seem to be on high alert.

253
00:16:21,330 --> 00:16:23,750
The mage either took it away, or made it disappear.

254
00:16:24,670 --> 00:16:26,370
It looks like there was an explosion.

255
00:16:27,050 --> 00:16:30,270
A fire was lit near the dragon's fuel sack, and it exploded.

256
00:16:30,270 --> 00:16:32,950
I'm shocked you survived.

257
00:16:33,350 --> 00:16:36,890
One of our party members used abjuration magic and protected us.

258
00:16:37,390 --> 00:16:38,590
So we were fine.

259
00:16:38,590 --> 00:16:41,850
You roll with a pretty good party, don't you?

260
00:16:42,310 --> 00:16:44,530
If you were there, you wouldn't be saying that.

261
00:16:44,970 --> 00:16:47,970
The person who did it had no idea she could use that spell.

262
00:16:48,610 --> 00:16:50,990
And later, our healer almost got us wiped out.

263
00:16:51,850 --> 00:16:56,470
Sure, it eventually worked out in the end, but if it hadn't, we would have looked like real fools.

264
00:16:57,710 --> 00:16:59,370
That's what I have to deal with.

265
00:16:59,370 --> 00:17:07,250
By the way, how exactly did you all manage to defeat the red dragon?

266
00:17:08,510 --> 00:17:10,010
Senshi and I distracted it.

267
00:17:10,430 --> 00:17:16,970
And then the tall man, his name's Laios, by the way, jumped onto it and struck its weak point, which finally took the red dragon down.

268
00:17:17,290 --> 00:17:18,450
That's pretty impressive.

269
00:17:19,570 --> 00:17:22,250
Courageousness is a good quality for a fighter to have.

270
00:17:22,910 --> 00:17:24,270
Oh, that wasn't courage.

271
00:17:24,270 --> 00:17:28,990
It was fine since we succeeded, but it was a dumb gamble.

272
00:17:29,850 --> 00:17:31,490
It really freaked me out.

273
00:17:32,030 --> 00:17:34,270
How can these people live so recklessly like that?

274
00:17:35,510 --> 00:17:38,190
We had two other party members who left our group.

275
00:17:40,690 --> 00:17:44,450
Thinking about it now, seems like they were probably the smart ones.

276
00:17:45,090 --> 00:17:48,650
I should have left then, but I guess I was too stubborn at the time.

277
00:17:50,010 --> 00:17:54,270
